Time and Space Complexity:
Time Complexity:
The time complexity depends on the number of combinations generated and the length of the candidates list.
In the worst case, the algorithm explores all possible combinations of numbers. Since we can repeat numbers, there are a maximum of O(2^n) possible combinations. Thus, the time complexity is O(2^n), where n is the number of candidates in the list.

Space Complexity:
The space complexity is O(k), where k is the maximum size of a combination (since we store each valid combination). Additionally, the recursion stack may also take O(k) space in the worst case.
Overall space complexity is O(k * 2^n) due to the storage of combinations in the result.

